chat_messages.text:
 The core issue is that **none of the review fields are `required`**, meaning you can save a completely empty review object `{}` to the database.

```javascript
// ❌ Current — all fields optional, empty review {} is valid
reviews: [{
    userId:  { type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: "User" },
    rating:  { type: Number, min: 1, max: 5 },
    comment: { type: String }
}],
```

```javascript
// ✅ Fixed
reviews: [{
    userId:  { 
        type:     mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, 
        ref:      "User", 
        required: true  // ← who wrote the review?
    },
    rating:  { 
        type:     Number, 
        min:      1, 
        max:      5, 
        required: true  // ← a review without a rating is meaningless
    },
    comment: { 
        type:      String, 
        maxlength: 500,   // ← unbounded string, anyone could dump 100KB of text
        trim:      true   // ← strip accidental whitespace
    }
}],
```

**All problems at a glance:**

| Field | Problem | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `userId` | Not required — anonymous ghost reviews possible | `required: true` |
| `rating` | Not required — a ratingless review is useless | `required: true` |
| `comment` | No `maxlength` — open to large payload abuse | `maxlength: 500` |
| `comment` | No `trim` — whitespace-only comments pass through | `trim: true` |
| All | No duplicate review guard | Add a validator (see below) |

One more thing — nothing stops the **same user from reviewing twice**. You'd catch that with a custom validator:

```javascript
reviews: [{
    userId:  { type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: "User", required: true },
    rating:  { type: Number, min: 1, max: 5, required: true },
    comment: { type: String, maxlength: 500, trim: true }
}],

// Prevent duplicate reviews from the same user
hospitalSchema.path("reviews").validate(function (reviews) {
    const ids = reviews.map(r => r.userId.toString());
    return ids.length === new Set(ids).size; // duplicate = Set smaller than array
}, "A user can only review once");
```

