**`donor.toObject()`:**
```javascript
// donor from mongoose is not a plain JS object
// it's a Mongoose Document with extra methods

donor.toObject()
// converts it to a plain JS object
// so you can manipulate it normally

// Before toObject:
donor → Mongoose Document (has .save(), .validate() etc)

// After toObject:
donor.toObject() → plain JS object { name, email, password, ... }
```

---

**`const { password: _, ...donorData }`:**
```javascript
// This is destructuring with renaming + rest operator

const { password: _, ...donorData } = donor.toObject()

// Breaking it down:
// password: _   → extract password, rename it to _ 
//                 (_ means "I'm taking this out but don't care about it")
// ...donorData  → put EVERYTHING ELSE into donorData

// Example:
const obj = { name: "Rahul", email: "r@g.com", password: "hashed123" }
const { password: _, ...rest } = obj

// _ = "hashed123"  ← extracted and discarded
// rest = { name: "Rahul", email: "r@g.com" }  ← no password ✅
```

