Can't extract geo keys... Point must be an array or object, 
instead got type missing
```

**The problem — `location` field in Donor model:**
```javascript
// Your Donor model has:
location: {
    type: { type: String, enum: ["Point"], default: "Point" },
    coordinates: { type: [Number], default: undefined }
}

// The 2dsphere index requires coordinates to exist
// When no location is sent → coordinates = undefined → index breaks
```

**Fix — two options:**

**Option 1 — remove 2dsphere index requirement for missing coords:**
```javascript
// In Donor.js change coordinates default:
coordinates: { 
    type:    [Number], 
    default: undefined,
    sparse:  true  // ← allows missing values
}

// And make the index sparse:
donorSchema.index({ location: "2dsphere" }, { sparse: true });
//                                            ↑ ignore docs without location
```

**Option 2 — send location in Postman (quick test fix):**
```json
{
    "name": "Rahul Sharma",
    "email": "rahulfads32@gmail.com",
    ...
    "location": {
        "type": "Point",
        "coordinates": [77.4126, 23.2599]
    }
}
```

---

**Option 1 is the right fix** — location should be optional for registration. Update your Donor model's index to sparse and try again!

